check 1: the battery is good enough
check 2: the image is the declared one, a whole boot partition, its AVB footer verifies
  the image names its root: system_a
check 3: the image's init accepts the slot it is booted from
check 4: the stored boot chain is whole, the ssh key is private and the reboot tool is the declared one
step 5: say what to expect
  One command, about 15 minutes: our boot image is flashed to the boot partition of the slot Android is NOT on (read two ways, built from device.toml's list "boot_a boot_b"), read back, and that slot is made active by the bootloader's own set_active - the call Android's OTA makes, a write to the GPT by the bootloader, with the slot flags and the GPT of its 6 disks read before and after. The phone then boots from the card and the lab logs in; then the way back, set_active of Android's slot, is made in the same run and the phone ends on Android. A stop at any step runs the way back.
check 6: the coordinator's go is recorded on the item for this image
step 7: the phone is on Android, adbd as root
check 8: adb reads the slot Android runs from
  adb: slot suffix _b
check 9: the boot partition to be flashed, read now, is its backup, or the declared image with the backup on file; the boot, dtbo and vbmeta partitions are hashed
  boot_a already holds the declared image (e337de53446aa98e4795e214648427e22b467b3ab39f2d208e201951ff4098f1); the stock backup is on file and hashes to its record (2a5cd3b20ef0da2b272d2dac460f868d4764d8bdb8cb426d62eee568f1344fb5): the flash can be undone
check 10: the GPT of every disk is read whole and kept
  6 disks' GPT kept, each whole with the right CRCs
step 11: take the phone to fastboot
check 12: fastboot agrees on the slot and the flash target is the other slot's boot partition
  Android runs from slot b; the one flash would be: fastboot -s SERIAL flash boot_a /home/mll/.local/share/agent-worktrees/google-walleye-lab/walleye-keeper-1795443037/build/images/NOT-TO-BOOT-ufs-on-images-ufs-root-booted-slot/NOT-TO-BOOT-ufs-on-ufs-root-booted-slot.img
check 13: the slot flags are read before
step 14: flash the boot partition of the slot Android is not on: one fastboot flash
step 15: the phone is on Android, adbd as root (Android's slot is still the active one)
check 16: the partition reads back as the image, and no other boot, dtbo or vbmeta partition changed
  boot_a reads back as the image; boot_a held the image already and the flash changed no partition
step 17: take the phone to fastboot
check 18: the flash reset only the flashed slot's successful and retry count
step 19: make the flashed slot active: the bootloader's own set_active
check 20: the flags changed as the bootloader's switch describes and nothing else
step 21: the new slot boots from the card and the lab logs in by ssh; its GPT is read
  no ssh from the new slot: sending the phone nothing; waiting up to 420 s for Android to answer adb, then the pstore is read first
  adb answered 0 s after the wait began
